  {
    "id": "1d156935023f6782fe3c438f",
    "path": "arrow_data::data::BufferSpec::FixedWidth",
    "name": "FixedWidth",
    "owner": "arrow_data::data::BufferSpec",
    "crate": "arrow-data",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "variant",
    "signature": "FixedWidth",
    "docs": "Each element is a fixed width primitive, with the given `byte_width` and `alignment`\n\n`alignment` is the alignment required by Rust for an array of the corresponding primitive,\nsee [`Layout::array`](std::alloc::Layout::array) and [`std::mem::align_of`].\n\nArrow-rs requires that all buffers have at least this alignment, to allow for\n[slice](std::slice) based APIs. Alignment in excess of this is not required to allow\nfor array slicing and interoperability with `Vec`, which cannot be over-aligned.\n\nNote that these alignment requirements will vary between architectures",
